# ar_net0 is the AR8030's native net_device, registered by artosyn_drv.ko
# itself (ar8030-transport kmod/artosyn_net.c, module param native_net=1,
# the default) as soon as the chip is running its RTOS firmware. No
# userspace bridge is involved any more: `ifup` opens bb socket slot 0
# port 3 on the chip, `ifdown` closes it. lifecycled's connected/dropped
# hooks (30-ifup.sh / 30-ifdown.sh) drive that, so nothing brings it up
# before there is an actual link to carry it.
#
# The peer still runs ar8030-tun (TAP, datagram mode, -p 3) -- the
# kernel side uses the same 0xab..0xbc datagram framing and Ethernet
# frames, so the two interoperate. slot 0 / port 3 has to match the
# peer's ar8030-tun invocation; see OpenIPC/sbc-groundstations' own
# package/ar8030/files/etc/network/interfaces.d/ar_net0. Port 3, not 2:
# port 2 is ar8030-transport-tx/-rx's own video socket.
#
# To go back to the userspace bridge instead: load artosyn_drv with
# native_net=0 and use the previous version of this file from git
# history (manual iface starting ar8030-tun -d ar_net0 -i 192.168.100.1
# -u 0 -p 3).
iface ar_net0 inet static
	address 192.168.100.1
	netmask 255.255.255.0
